WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:07.120
It's been just over twelve years since the first&nbsp;
Twilight film exploded across movie screens.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:12.960
Despite the series' status as a box-office&nbsp;
powerhouse, there are plenty of questionable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.960
instances in the films that you might&nbsp;
have missed when you were a teenager.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.680
Before he first appeared in the&nbsp;
Twilight series as Jacob Black,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:27.280
Bella's second love interest and burgeoning&nbsp;
werewolf, actor Taylor Lautner was best known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:33.120
for his role in The Adventures of Sharkboy&nbsp;
and Lavagirl. Jacob wasn't a major character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:37.680
in the first Twilight film, but one&nbsp;
detail stands out during his scenes.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:42.320
Jacob's character initially has long&nbsp;
hair that reaches past his shoulders.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:47.200
Since Lautner had short hair, he had to&nbsp;
wear a pretty obvious wig for the role.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:51.920
Team Jacob teens might've been able to turn&nbsp;
a blind eye to the hairpiece when the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:58.400
film was released, but it's pretty hard to miss as&nbsp;
an adult. Not only was the wig super-noticeable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:03.760
but Lautner said that the wig also caused&nbsp;
numerous technical issues on set. Whenever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:09.520
stray hairs would fly into his face the crew&nbsp;
would have to cut and start the scene over.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:13.840
Lautner also said there was mutual&nbsp;
hatred between him and his wig,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:18.080
and that he didn't miss it after&nbsp;
the series ended. Luckily for him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:23.360
Jacob's character cropped his hair after his&nbsp;
transformation into a werewolf in New Moon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:28.480
so he was able to part ways with the wig for&nbsp;
the rest of the series. According to Lautner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:32.960
they even gave the wig its own round of&nbsp;
applause when its role officially wrapped.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:39.497
This is more of a fun "blink and you'll miss it"&nbsp;
sort of goof, but it becomes more obvious when you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.497 --> 00:01:45.360
rewatch the series as an adult. Shortly after&nbsp;
Bella first meets Edward at Forks High School,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:50.960
Edward comes to her rescue when a van careens&nbsp;
toward her in the school parking lot. In the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:56.240
scene, Bella is shocked at the impossibility&nbsp;
of Edward's actions, from darting across the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:01.200
parking lot instantly to stopping the force of&nbsp;
the van with his arm. It's one of the pair's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:07.200
first encounters, and also the first hint for&nbsp;
Bella that Edward is not your average teenager.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:13.360
But one detail that bothers viewers is a small&nbsp;
prop in this scene. Just before the van spins out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:18.480
of control, Bella is putting things into her&nbsp;
backpack -- which is on the hood of her car.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:23.120
While Edward prevents the van from crushing&nbsp;
Bella, it still hits the back of her truck&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:28.480
with considerable force. However, when the&nbsp;
film cuts to a wider shot of the parking lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:33.280
as students rush to check on Bella, the&nbsp;
backpack is still in the exact place it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:39.360
was before the crash. In a real life scenario,&nbsp;
her bag probably would have been sent flying or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:44.000
would have at least fallen to the ground.&nbsp;
This was most likely a continuity error,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:49.840
or Bella must have had a super strong magnet&nbsp;
in her backpack that held it in place.

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:55.600
A huge plot point in the Twilight books is that&nbsp;
while Bella wants to sleep with Edward, he refuses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.600 --> 00:03:02.320
to do so until they get married. Repressed desire&nbsp;
also exists in other forms in the Twilight saga:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:07.600
the Cullens naturally desire human blood but&nbsp;
cannot drink it, while Edward is naturally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:13.120
drawn to Bella because she's the only person who&nbsp;
can resist his ability to read people's thoughts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:18.320
Edward's reasoning for not wanting to sleep&nbsp;
with Bella has to do with his superhuman vampire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:23.760
strength: He believes his desire is dangerous&nbsp;
for Bella, and that he could actually hurt her.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:28.720
Edward's views are not that surprising&nbsp;
given some context about his creator.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:33.760
The author of the Twilight books, Stephenie&nbsp;
Meyer, is a devout Mormon and has said that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:38.640
her characters exhibit her own beliefs&nbsp;
and feelings about premarital relations.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:44.560
Even actor Robert Pattinson, who portrayed Edward&nbsp;
in the films, agreed that despite the steamy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:50.080
chemistry between him and his co-star Kristen&nbsp;
Stewart, the movie's themes are very chaste.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:55.360
Victoria was one of the longest running&nbsp;
antagonists for Bella and the Cullens throughout&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.360 --> 00:04:01.200
the series. In the first film, her mate James is&nbsp;
killed by the Cullens after he attempts to kill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:07.280
Bella. Victoria managed to slip away amidst all&nbsp;
the chaos, but she came back looking for revenge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:13.440
in New Moon. During the first two films, Victoria&nbsp;
was portrayed by Rachelle Lefevre, who reportedly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:18.880
prepared for the role by pretending to be a&nbsp;
cat to match Victoria's agility and demeanor.

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:24.160
When the third film, Eclipse, was announced, it&nbsp;
was assumed Lefevre would reprise her role as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:29.440
Victoria. However, the part was recast due&nbsp;
to a scheduling conflict between Eclipse's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:33.760
shooting schedule and Lefevre's commitment&nbsp;
to shooting the movie Barney's Version.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:38.640
The two films' schedules overlapped&nbsp;
by 10 days, and Summit — the studio&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:44.080
behind the Twilight films — was unable to&nbsp;
change the shoot to accommodate Lefevre.

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:49.840
The role eventually went to Bryce Dallas Howard,&nbsp;
who had previously turned it down because it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:55.200
too small a part. Lefevre was understandably&nbsp;
upset by the whole series of events,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:59.200
but Summit was not willing to&nbsp;
budge in its decision to recast.

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:05.840
The cover of the novel Twilight is a dramatically&nbsp;
lit image of two hands holding an apple. Apples&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:10.480
are traditionally a symbol of the forbidden&nbsp;
fruit of knowledge and, by extension,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:15.760
desire. Stephenie Meyer also confirmed that&nbsp;
the apple on the book's cover was a deliberate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:20.960
biblical allusion. Themes of forbidden fruit&nbsp;
are consistent throughout the Twilight series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:26.400
and many characters are drawn to or&nbsp;
desire things or people they cannot have.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:31.760
If you watch closely, actor Robert Pattinson&nbsp;
recreated the now infamous Twilight cover&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:37.440
during a scene in the first film. In the scene,&nbsp;
Bella drops an apple on the floor. The apple then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:43.520
bounces off Edward's foot and perfectly lands in&nbsp;
his two palms. The whole thing happens in just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:49.600
a few seconds, but super attentive fans were&nbsp;
able to notice and appreciate this Easter egg.

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:52.320
Since vampires don't sleep,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:57.760
it only makes sense for Edward Cullen to break&nbsp;
into Bella's house and watch her sleep, right?

00:05:58.400 --> 00:05:59.360
"Do you do that a lot?"

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.040
"Just the last couple of months"

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:08.560
Edward encroaching on Bella's privacy rubbed&nbsp;
some people the wrong way when they first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:14.560
encountered the series as teens. As adults, we&nbsp;
surely see his actions as straight-up creepy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:19.040
and gross. It would be weird if&nbsp;
they were already in a relationship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:23.680
but they weren't even dating at this&nbsp;
point! This is often the first bit of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:28.800
evidence given when discussing how unsettling&nbsp;
Edward's behavior is throughout the series.

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:34.800
Robert Pattinson's film depiction of Edward&nbsp;
doesn't exactly help his ominous image either,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:39.920
as he spent most of the first Twilight&nbsp;
film staring intently at his love interest.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:42.880
Bella reads Edward's mannerisms as mysterious,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:47.200
and they inspired millions of teenage&nbsp;
readers to fall in love with him. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:53.520
it goes without saying that if he were a real&nbsp;
person he'd be covered in giant red flags.

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:59.680
He's also super possessive and controlling of&nbsp;
Bella, consistently leaving her out of major&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:04.400
points of decision-making in their relationship.&nbsp;
When Bella is attacked by a fellow member&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:09.520
of Edward's coven, he decides for her that&nbsp;
their relationship is too dangerous for her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:15.440
Rather than letting Bella assess and accept any&nbsp;
risks for herself, Edward puts the situation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:20.720
solely in his control, which ultimately ends&nbsp;
up sending her into a depressive spiral.

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:25.680
The anatomy of vampires in the Twilight&nbsp;
films is pretty straightforward.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:30.000
Their skin is impervious to sharp&nbsp;
objects, they sparkle in direct&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:33.360
sunlight, and they don't have&nbsp;
blood running through their veins.

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:38.160
The only thing supposedly sharp enough&nbsp;
to break vampire skin is vampire teeth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:40.480
which are used throughout the Twilight films&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:45.600
as weapons against enemy vampires -- and&nbsp;
as medical instruments in Breaking Dawn.

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:51.760
So if vampire skin cannot be broken, how does&nbsp;
James have a tattoo in the first Twilight film?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:55.760
While fans may not have thought about it&nbsp;
too much when they became obsessed with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.760 --> 00:08:00.720
the films for the first time, it definitely&nbsp;
doesn't make sense upon closer inspection.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:04.080
If a scalpel couldn't break a&nbsp;
vampire's skin in Breaking Dawn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:08.720
a tattoo needle definitely wouldn't&nbsp;
be able to place ink in the skin.

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:13.680
The answer to this mystery is pretty&nbsp;
straightforward: the actor who portrayed James,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:19.360
Cam Gigandet, has a tattoo, and the film&nbsp;
didn't think it was necessary to cover it up.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:24.320
James' tattoo wasn't exactly an important&nbsp;
element to his part of the story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:27.600
so the creators of the film&nbsp;
just decided to let it slide.

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:31.600
There's a lot going on in Breaking Dawn: Part 2,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:36.400
but there definitely should have been more&nbsp;
screen time devoted to discussing how Jacob,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:41.440
Bella's longtime friend and former love&nbsp;
interest, imprinted on her newborn baby.

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:45.200
"You nicknamed my daughter&nbsp;
after the Loch Ness Monster!!?"

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:48.960
A lot of Jacob fans simply wrote&nbsp;
his newfound protectiveness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:53.920
and bond with Renesmee off as romantic,&nbsp;
but there's a bit more to it than that.

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:58.240
Jacob's reveal that Bella's baby is&nbsp;
his soulmate is a moment that's been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:03.280
the subject of countless memes and analysis,&nbsp;
but a lot of people who watched the films as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:09.920
teens have even more questions about this plot&nbsp;
twist now as adults. Even if Renesmee grows up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:14.960
faster than normal humans, wouldn't Jacob&nbsp;
be essentially grooming her from childhood?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:21.200
What's the exact science behind imprinting? Why&nbsp;
doesn't anyone else in the Cullen clan see any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:27.520
major issues with this? Does Renesmee have any&nbsp;
agency in this huge part of her life at all?

00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:34.000
In the films, Jacob's imprinting on Renesmee is&nbsp;
kind of just explained away by attributing it to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:39.600
ambiguous werewolf idiosyncrasies. That might&nbsp;
have been enough for teenagers watching the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:45.520
film the first time, but definitely would earn&nbsp;
more scrutiny from those same viewers today.

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:52.160
While Stephenie Meyer was a household name by the&nbsp;
time the first Twilight film flooded movie screens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:58.080
worldwide, not too many people were familiar with&nbsp;
Meyer's physical appearance. Little did fans know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:03.920
that they could easily find the creator of their&nbsp;
favorite series right within the film adaptations.

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:09.280
Towards the end of Twilight, there's a scene where&nbsp;
Bella and her father are eating at the local Forks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:15.040
diner. The camera pans past a woman sitting&nbsp;
at the diner counter typing away at a laptop.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:20.560
Super attentive fans were able to recognize&nbsp;
this anonymous writer as Stephenie Meyer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:24.480
but it was subtle enough that more&nbsp;
casual viewers might have missed it.

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:30.320
Meyer also had a second cameo in Breaking Dawn:&nbsp;
Part 1, during Bella and Edward's wedding. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:35.520
wedding scene had huge hype leading up to the&nbsp;
film's release, and when Bella walks down the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:40.960
aisle, you can see Stephenie Meyer standing among&nbsp;
all the other wedding guests at the ceremony.

00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:45.680
Although Stephenie Meyer said she had to be&nbsp;
talked into participating in the film shoots,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:49.760
her fans probably appreciated seeing&nbsp;
their favorite author on screen.

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:53.920
According to the world of&nbsp;
Twilight, keeping the existence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:59.280
of vampires secret is crucial to&nbsp;
any vampire's survival. The Volturi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:04.080
a large coven of Vampires who reside in&nbsp;
Italy, are recognized as the official&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:09.360
leaders of vampire society and enforce the&nbsp;
rules that are used to maintain secrecy.

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:14.400
Vampires in the Twilight universe are expected&nbsp;
to follow the coven's laws, and those who break&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:20.160
the rules are typically punished with death.&nbsp;
Such rules include avoiding direct sunlight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:25.360
since vampire skin would sparkle and quickly&nbsp;
draw the attention of any humans nearby.

00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:29.040
However, despite the Cullens&nbsp;
carefully adapting their lifestyle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:33.840
to keep a relatively low profile within&nbsp;
Forks, there are still plenty of times&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:38.720
where a reasonable person should have&nbsp;
noticed that something was a little off.

00:11:38.720 --> 00:11:43.440
For example, while the Cullens explain to&nbsp;
Bella that they settled in Forks because of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:48.960
how constantly rainy and cloudy the climate is,&nbsp;
there are still a few times that the vampires&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:54.560
were exposed to direct sunlight in front of other&nbsp;
humans. When Bella sees the Cullens for the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.560 --> 00:12:00.560
time, they all sit down at a cafeteria table&nbsp;
together by a window, where a tiny bit of sun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.560 --> 00:12:07.760
filters in through the glass. In this moment, you&nbsp;
can see a bit of light on Alice's arm. You'd think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:13.440
that for people whose lives depend on avoiding&nbsp;
the sun they'd sit further away from windows.

